@startuml
title ASUC-04b - Adapt to energy conditions: act and give feedback (UC4)
autonumber "<b>00"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam dpi 140
skinparam maxMessageSize 170
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #555555
  LifeLineBorderColor #999999
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFF4F4
  ParticipantBorderColor #B52330
  ActorBackgroundColor #EEEEEE
  ActorBorderColor #202025
  GroupBorderColor #B52330
}
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FAF5F5
skinparam NoteBorderColor #B52330

actor "Time\nTrigger" as TT
participant "Event\nBus" as EB
participant "Job\nScheduler" as JS
participant "Policy\nEngine" as POL
database "Data\nStore" as DB
participant "Forecast\nWorker" as FW
participant "Forecast Model\nAdapter" as AD
participant "Model\nRouter" as RT
participant "Model\nEvaluator" as ME
actor "System\nOperator" as OP
participant "Operator\nConsole" as OC
participant "Telemetry" as TEL

== Notification (when the mode changes) ==
EB -> JS : modeChanged(from, to, reason)
EB -> RT : modeChanged(from, to, reason)
RT -> RT : drop cache entries whose lifetime class no longer matches the mode

== Consumer 1: forecast refresh ==
TT -> JS : tick()
JS -> POL : current()
POL --> JS : mode, concurrency, deadline window
JS -> DB : claimDueJobs(limit = concurrency) with a lease
DB --> JS : jobs with deadline and remaining time
loop each claimed job
  JS -> JS : decide(job, mode):\ndeadline reached -> RUN in any mode;\nGREEN -> RUN; AMBER -> RUN only if at most half of the window remains;\notherwise DEFER
  alt decision = RUN
    JS -> FW : run(job)
    FW -> DB : readObservations(product)
    DB --> FW : price series
    FW -> AD : predict(series, 7 days)
    AD --> FW : forecast
    FW -> FW : sanity check: non-negative, within plausible bounds of recent prices
    alt check failed or model error
      FW --> JS : failed (the previous forecast stays visible with its age)
    else check passed
      FW -> DB : save forecast (model id, generatedAt, status)
      FW --> JS : done, duration
    end
    JS -> JS : estimate energy and emissions:\nkWh := power * duration / 3.6e6; gCO2e := kWh * intensity at start
  else decision = DEFER
    JS -> DB : release the lease, set the next check before the deadline
  end
  JS -> DB : write the job execution log (decision, reason, mode, intensity, kWh, gCO2e)
  JS -> TEL : decisions, deferrals, deadline overrides, forecast age
end

== Consumer 2: AI routing ==
RT -> POL : current() (cached up to 60 s; the event only makes the change visible earlier)
POL --> RT : operating mode and routing class
RT -> RT : GREEN: small (local) model, escalate to the large model;\nAMBER: small model or template;\nRED: cache or template only, answer labelled "simplified"

== Consumer 3: optional batches ==
ME -> POL : current()
POL --> ME : operating mode
ME -> ME : model evaluation and import backfills run only in GREEN\n(at most 7 days of deferral); the mandatory daily import is never deferred
ME -> TEL : evaluationDeferred() or evaluationFinished()

== Feedback ==
OP -> OC : open the dashboards
OC -> TEL : getDashboards()
TEL --> OC : mode timeline, signals, deferrals, placements, kWh, gCO2e,\nimmediate-run baseline
OC --> OP : show the comparison
note over JS, TEL
  Placement of the flexible workloads follows the same mode event (sequence ASUC-04c).
  A deadline forces an execution attempt, not a guaranteed result.
  Lower emissions are an outcome to measure, not a property of the design (NFR-10).
end note
@enduml
